            <h2 class="section-title">Healthcare Accounting in Delhi: GST Segregation, ITC, and Medical Compliance</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - Healthcare Accounting Services in Delhi Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>Healthcare accounting = exempt/taxable GST segregation + ITC reversal for mixed supplies + doctor ITR (S.44ADA) + pharmacy inventory + Ayushman Bharat reconciliation. Most clinical services GST-exempt (Notification 12/2017). Room rent >Rs 5,000/day: 5% GST. Cosmetic: 18%. Standalone diagnostics: 18%. Delhi = India's medical capital (AIIMS, Apollo, Fortis, Max). 82+ Ayushman Bharat hospitals. No PT. From Rs 8,000/month.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi is India's medical capital with unique accounting complexity. For a comprehensive overview, see our <a href="/healthcare-sector-accounting-services">Healthcare Accounting</a> national guide.</p><div class="table-responsive-wrapper"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GST Exemption</td><td>Core clinical services exempt (SAC 9993). Room rent >Rs 5,000/day: 5%. Cosmetic: 18%</td></tr><tr><td>Applicable To</td><td>Hospitals, clinics, nursing homes, diagnostics, pharmacies, telemedicine</td></tr><tr><td>Key Compliance</td><td>Exempt/taxable segregation; ITC reversal (S.17(2)); TDS on doctors (S.194J)</td></tr><tr><td>Cost From</td><td>Rs 8,000/month (clinic); Rs 20,000/month (hospital)</td></tr><tr><td>Penalty Risk</td><td>Rs 25,000 no books (S.271A); Rs 10,000+ wrong GST (S.122 CGST)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p</p>
                <p>AIIMS ranked 97th globally. 82+ Ayushman Bharat hospitals. Apollo, Fortis, Max, BLK, Sir Ganga Ram. 30,000+ beds. $9B medical tourism. 5 GST zones. No PT. Patron's Rohini office handles all Delhi zones with healthcare-specialist CAs.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
