<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Are Healthcare Accounting Services?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Specialised financial recording, compliance, and reporting for hospitals, clinics, diagnostics, and medical practices under CGST Act 2017, IT Act 1961, and Clinical Establishments Act 2010.</p><p><strong>Key difference:</strong> Must maintain separate revenue streams for GST-exempt clinical services, taxable room rent, pharmacy sales, cafeteria, parking. A 200-bed hospital needs each transaction classified correctly.</p><p><strong>Delhi context:</strong> Medical tourism ($9B → $13B by 2026 under Heal in India). International patient billing, forex receipts, export-of-service under GST. 5 commissionerate zones.</p><p>See <a href="/accounting-services">Accounting Services</a> for general business accounting.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Healthcare Accounting Services in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>SAC 9993:</strong> Service Accounting Code for healthcare. Core clinical services exempt under Notification 12/2017-CT(R).</p><p><strong>Section 17(2) CGST:</strong> ITC reversal for mixed supplies. Hospitals with exempt + taxable must reverse ITC proportionally monthly.</p><p><strong>Section 194J:</strong> TDS at 10% on visiting consultant/doctor professional fees. Monthly deduction, quarterly filing.</p><p><strong>Section 44ADA:</strong> Presumptive taxation for doctors. 50% of gross receipts as income, up to Rs 75L (95% digital).</p><p><strong>Room Rent Threshold:</strong> Hospital room >Rs 5,000/day (excl ICU/CCU/NICU) attracts 5% GST without ITC.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
